      "text": "Let's go through this problem step by step:\n\nGiven: The difference when the product of 4 (which can be represented as the number, \\( n \\)) and the positive number \\( n \\) is subtracted from 16 is greater than 10.\n\n1. Translate the given statement into a mathematical inequality:\n\\[ 16 - 4n > 10 \\]\n\n2. Simplify the inequality step by step:\n\\[ 16 - 4n > 10 \\]\n\\[ -4n > 10 - 16 \\]\n\\[ -4n > -6 \\]\n\n3. Divide both sides of the inequality by -4, remembering to reverse the inequality sign when dividing by a negative number:\n\\[ n < \\frac{-6}{-4} \\]\n\\[ n < \\frac{3}{2} \\]\n\n4. Since \\( n \\) must be a positive integer, find out the possible values for \\( n \\):\n\\[ n = 1, 2 \\]\n\n5. Confirm each value of \\( n \\) in the original inequality:\n- For \\( n = 1 \\):\n\\[ 16 - 4(1) = 12 \\]\n\\[ 12 > 10 \\]\nThis satisfies the condition.\n\n- For \\( n = 2 \\):\n\\[ 16 - 4(2) = 8 \\]\n\\[ 8 > 10 \\]\nThis does not satisfy the condition.\n\nThus, only \\( n = 1 \\) satisfies the given conditions, so there is only \\(\\boxed{1}\\) positive integer that satisfies the conditions.",
