      "text": "To solve the problem, we start by defining the variable and expressing the given conditions mathematically. Let's denote the unknown number by \\( x \\).\n\n1. The product of 4 and the number is \\( 4x \\).\n2. The difference when this product is subtracted from 16 is \\( 16 - 4x \\).\n\nAccording to the problem, this difference must be greater than 10. Therefore, we can write the inequality:\n\\[\n16 - 4x > 10\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve this inequality step by step.\n\n1. Subtract 16 from both sides to isolate the term \\( -4x \\):\n\\[\n16 - 4x - 16 > 10 - 16\n\\]\n\\[\n-4x > -6\n\\]\n\n2. Divide both sides of the inequality by -4. Remember that dividing by a negative number reverses the inequality sign:\n\\[\nx < \\frac{6}{4}\n\\]\n\\[\nx < 1.5\n\\]\n\nSince \\( x \\) must be a positive integer, the only positive integers that satisfy \\( x < 1.5 \\) are \\( x = 1 \\) and \\( x = 0 \\). However, \\( x = 0 \\) is not a positive integer, so the only positive integer that satisfies the condition is \\( x = 1 \\).\n\nTherefore, the number of positive integers that satisfy the given conditions is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]",
